2026-03-30T04:26:48Z theme=remote-cfar-batching-root-cause

plan:
- compare deployed direct dotnet-fsi vs single EvalInteraction vs smarter paragraph batching
- determine whether remote Running is due to async bookkeeping or FSI interaction batching
- document only hard conclusions

results:
- direct dotnet fsi on rewritten script inside deployed container: completed in 333899 ms
- single giant EvalInteraction on same payload: timeout at 420 s
- paragraph/top-level batching with EvalInteraction: completed in 316735 ms
- post-init query on same session after paragraph batching: succeeded

conclusion:
- root cause is overly coarse splitInteractionBatch behavior, not async registry or missing result synchronization
- large .fsx-like payloads need top-level paragraph batching before EvalInteraction
- source fix applied in Akka.FSI.Supervisor/FsiWorker.fs

notes:
- separate local supervisor validation hit an unrelated FsPicklerTextSerializer method mismatch
- that dependency issue is not the primary cause of the live CFar Running symptom
